WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.368
What? You think 'cause I went
to rehab, I stayed clean?

00:00:02.468 --> 00:00:03.970
I mean, ain't that the point?

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:05.205
♪ (CONTEMPLATIVE MUSIC PLAYS) ♪

00:00:05.305 --> 00:00:07.172
Yeah, well,
the world's coming to an end

00:00:07.273 --> 00:00:09.542
and I haven't even
graduated high school yet.

00:00:10.343 --> 00:00:13.179 line:0%
I'm Dr. Ali Mattu,
cognitive behavioral therapist,

00:00:13.279 --> 00:00:15.848 line:0%
and I'm here today
in collaboration with HBO

00:00:15.948 --> 00:00:20.186
<i> to offer my take on themes
of mental health in their shows.</i>

00:00:20.286 --> 00:00:23.222
(SLURRED) I'm just so happy.

00:00:23.322 --> 00:00:25.090
Today, we'll talk
about substance use

00:00:25.191 --> 00:00:26.592
<i> and how it can affect behavior</i>

00:00:26.692 --> 00:00:29.162
<i> through the lens of Rue
 in</i> Euphoria.

00:00:31.164 --> 00:00:32.731
RUE BENNETT:<i> If I could be
 a different person,</i>

00:00:32.831 --> 00:00:34.567
<i> I promise you, I would.</i>

00:00:35.434 --> 00:00:39.572
<i> Euphoria</i> is one of the most
honest representations

00:00:39.672 --> 00:00:42.509
<i> of substance use problems
 I've seen.</i>

00:00:43.009 --> 00:00:46.813
Rue talks about her history
with grief,

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:51.083
<i> with a learning disability
 and anxiety.</i>

00:00:51.184 --> 00:00:52.818
RUE:<i> All of a sudden,
 I couldn't breathe.</i>

00:00:53.386 --> 00:00:55.288
<i> They gave me liquid Valium.</i>

00:00:55.955 --> 00:00:57.156
And I found a way to live.

00:00:57.523 --> 00:01:00.559
Some people might be vulnerable
to developing problems

00:01:00.659 --> 00:01:01.394
with substances,

00:01:01.994 --> 00:01:05.498
<i> because they're experiencing
 underlying mental illness.</i>

00:01:05.598 --> 00:01:07.866
FEZCO: I don't know
what type of fucked up shit

00:01:07.967 --> 00:01:09.869
you got going inside your head.

00:01:09.969 --> 00:01:11.370
And I don't know how to help.

00:01:11.470 --> 00:01:13.640
But I could tell you
one thing...

00:01:14.007 --> 00:01:16.342
This drug shit
is not the answer.

00:01:16.442 --> 00:01:18.511
The stereotype that exists
in our country

00:01:18.611 --> 00:01:23.182
is certain people are addicts
and will always be addicts.

00:01:23.282 --> 00:01:24.984
<i> And that's just not true.</i>

00:01:25.085 --> 00:01:27.787
<i> As we treat the underlying
 mental illness,</i>

00:01:28.087 --> 00:01:30.689
substance use can often
resolve itself.

00:01:31.023 --> 00:01:32.491
<i>This is something we can all do.</i>

00:01:32.592 --> 00:01:36.729
Have compassion,
and in a judgment-free way...

00:01:40.266 --> 00:01:43.903
<i>This seems like a radical idea.</i>

00:01:44.003 --> 00:01:46.172
You'd be surprised at how

00:01:46.473 --> 00:01:48.640
most people never get asked
this question.

00:01:49.007 --> 00:01:50.243
<i> And it opens the door.</i>

00:01:50.343 --> 00:01:53.045
<i> It makes it easier for them
 to talk about</i>

00:01:53.146 --> 00:01:55.381
<i> what the substances are doing
 and also,</i>

00:01:55.481 --> 00:01:58.250
<i> get them to be open to talking
 about change.</i>

00:01:58.584 --> 00:01:59.952
<i>That's all I have for you today.</i>

00:02:00.052 --> 00:02:01.954
And remember,
if you need help,

00:02:02.054 --> 00:02:04.357
there are resources available
to you.

00:02:05.224 --> 00:02:06.325
<i> I'm Dr. Ali Mattu,</i>

00:02:06.425 --> 00:02:08.394
<i> and I'll see you
 in the next video.</i>

00:02:12.164 --> 00:02:13.733
♪ (MUSIC CONCLUDES) ♪

